# The bootstrap tools the container test image installs before the locked
# dependency set (tools/container/Dockerfile).
#
# uv and pyOCD are pinned exactly because the tests read what these two
# programs print and write: uv's receipt layout and pyOCD's no-probe refusal
# are what the fixtures under tests/fixtures reproduce, so a release that
# changes either should fail the drift tests on a deliberate bump with a test
# run behind it, not on a rebuild. setuptools and wheel are the build backend
# this project declares, and the tests build wheels of the checkout with
# `--no-isolation`, so the build needs no network of its own.
#
# The lock file beside this one carries the hashes the image installs with, so
# a compromised release of any of these or of anything they pull in cannot
# enter the image that the required container check runs in.
#
# Regenerate the hash-pinned lock file after editing:
#   uv pip compile --generate-hashes --universal --python-version 3.12 requirements/container.in -o requirements/container.txt
uv==0.12.9
pyocd==0.45.1
setuptools>=77
wheel
